TITLE: Basics of Open Mobile OS

SECTION:
HEADER: This help chapter will cover the following
TEXT:
- Opening and closing an app
- Moving things in an out of folders
- Navigating the system

SECTION:
HEADER: Opening and closing an app
TEXT:
To open an app, simply:
- Click on the icon
Dragging it will not open it

When closing an app, you would want to
- If a keyboard is open, close it
- Pull down from the top of the screen, this will open up the TopBarManager
- Click the red button
You are now at the desktop!!

SECTION:
HEADER: Moving objects in and out of folders
TEXT:
To make a folder
- Press the + at the bottom of the screen
- Choose and type a name
Congratulations you made a folder

To place apps in the folder:
- Simply drag the app into the folder icon
- If successful a notification will appear

To take an app out of the folder:
- Drag it out of place
- If successful a notification will appear



SECTION:
HEADER: Navigating the system
TEXT:
Depending on how many icons you have on the screen, you may need to change page

On the desktop(No Folder):
- Swipe left or right, to go to the desired folder

In a folder:
- Swipe down and up

To open a folder:
- Simply click the white icon with four icons inside

To exit a folder:
- Click the back button on the top left of the screen



